<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andriamanelo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andriamanelo was a Merina king of the central highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, traditionally dated to the mid-sixteenth century. Royal tradition credits him with subduing the earlier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vazimba">Vazimba</a> inhabitants with iron-tipped spears, founding the line of Merina kings and building fortified hill towns surrounded by ditches. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ralambo">Ralambo</a> is said to have given the kingdom the name Imerina.</p></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Oral histories make Andriamanelo the eldest son of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vazimba">Vazimba</a> queen, named as Rafohy or Rangita, and her Hova husband Manelobe, who may have come from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zafiraminia">Zafiraminia</a> people of Anosy. The Hova were then a minority clan lately arrived in the Vazimba highlands from the south-east. To prevent the kingdom from splitting, the queens decreed that Andriamanelo would inherit the crown and be succeeded by his younger brother Andriamananitany, a rule called fanjakana arindra. While his mother lived he was given the village of Alasora to rule.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Reign</h2><p>Andriamanelo extended his lands from Alasora south to Merimanjaka north, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vazimba">Vazimba</a> stronghold of Analamanga, which divided his realm, resisted him and fell only to his grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrianjaka">Andrianjaka</a>. He fortified Alasora with dry moats (hadivory), trenches (hadifetsy) and gates closed by a great rolled stone disc (vavahady). Iron implements, however, were in use in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> at least four centuries before his war, and astrology had come to the island through contact with Arab seafarers; he may rather have been among the first rulers in Imerina to use such things widely.</p><p>His brother copied his fortifications at a village of his own, abandoned it under Andriamanelo's anger and was then killed by a group of Hova, possibly on the king's order. In remorse Andriamanelo married his sister Rafotsindrindramanjaka to his brother's son and decreed that their daughter's child by his own son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ralambo">Ralambo</a> would rule after Ralambo. He married his cousin Ramaitsoanala, daughter of King Rabiby of Ambohidrabiby, which brought him those lands; six of their children died, and only the seventh, Ralambo, survived. Tradition also credits him with founding the andriana as a class of nobles and the marriage gift of vodiondry, the hindquarters of a sheep.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>Andriamanelo died at an advanced age around 1575 and was buried at Alasora in an earthen ditch. Tradition places his tomb south-east of the royal compound rather than to the north as was customary, perhaps to mark his mixed descent, and a similar tomb to the north may be his mother's. These two are the oldest known royal-style tombs in Imerina. The circumcision rite credited to him was kept by the Merina monarchy to the end of the 19th century.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Andriamanelo” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Royal traditions, the Tantara ny Andriana compiled in the nineteenth century, credit <b>Andriamanelo</b>, conventionally dated to the mid-sixteenth century, with subduing the earlier Vazimba inhabitants with iron-tipped spears and founding the line of Merina kings, and his son Ralambo with giving the kingdom its name, its royal talismans…</blockquote><a href="/empire/merina-kingdom">Merina Kingdom · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
